                                        "entry_id": "58e6370c-49b9-3791-84ee-053abf0e4b67",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In an inherent way; naturally, innately."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "11ceeb7e-c63a-45b1-b3f5-aac65106c8bf",
                                                "sense_id": "ebad639d-f63a-3bae-a9d5-dbd0dad2293e",
                                                "text": "Rights are inherently in all the inhabitants; but charters, by annulling those rights, in the majority, leave the right, by exclusion, in the hands of a few."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d00f1383-94ee-4d98-a34c-73ba85e127ca",
                                                "sense_id": "ebad639d-f63a-3bae-a9d5-dbd0dad2293e",
                                                "text": "Democrats are quick to say that President Donald Trump’s tariffs are horrible, awful, terrible. But Democrats are also stressing that they are not inherently anti-tariff."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "5d8a1b1f-46a7-44cb-9835-5b36139101e7",
                        "source_entry_id": "bbfde287-ea88-34a1-910e-36e64a82889b",
